Package: trestle
Version: 0.1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Brian Miller <brianthomasmiller@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: 255
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.38), libjson-c5 (>= 0.15), nftables
Recommends: aardvark-dns
Suggests: podman, containernetworking-plugins
Section: net
Priority: optional
Description: CNI and Netavark plugin attaching rootless containers to host bridges
 trestle lets rootless Podman containers (through Netavark) and Kubernetes
 pods (through CNI) attach to a bridge on the host. An unprivileged plugin
 validates each request and hands it, together with the container's network
 namespace, to the trestled daemon, which checks the caller against
 per-network user and group lists, creates the bridge and veth pair, assigns
 addresses, publishes host names (/etc/hosts, dnsmasq, aardvark-dns) and
 manages nftables filtering and masquerading.
